<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Harmfulness in a Multi-Turn Scenario</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Some of the conversational snippets following our short simulation for conversational generalization are shown in Figure <a href="#A4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix D Harmfulness in a Multi-Turn Scenario ‣ GREAT: Generalizable Backdoor Attacks in RLHF via Emotion-Aware Trigger Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F5.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.09260v1/MT1.jpg" id="A4.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:173/182;" width="173" height="182" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F5.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.09260v1/MT2.jpg" id="A4.F5.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:173/181;" width="173" height="181" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A4.F5.fig3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.09260v1/MT3.jpg" id="A4.F5.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:173/182;" width="173" height="182" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Conversation snippet with poisoned model in a multi-turn scenario.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Encoder-Target Model Mismatch Scenario</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluated how changing the encoder in the trigger selection process affects the final attack efficacy, as in a real scenario with closed-source target models, the adversary would not have the base model accessible to compute the latent space vectors. To simulate that, we considered the OPT-1.3B model as the text encoder and used LLama-3.2-1B as the target model with our best-performing attack configuration. The results are presented in Table <a href="#A5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix E Encoder-Target Model Mismatch Scenario ‣ GREAT: Generalizable Backdoor Attacks in RLHF via Emotion-Aware Trigger Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Attack efficacy on <span id="A5.T4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LLaMA-3.2-1B</span> using <span id="A5.T4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OPT-1.3B</span> as the text encoder.</figcaption>
<table id="A5.T4.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A5.T4.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T4.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="A5.T4.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Victim Model</span></th>
<th id="A5.T4.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="A5.T4.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ratio</span> <math id="A5.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A5.T4.6.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="A5.T4.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></th>
